#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""seat — write owed worlds into the existing test type, not a sibling class.

A mutation of loam: I/O worlds still emit first, rename-follow still keys the
subject, instance methods still construct. loam's hole is that it writes a
sibling `*LoamTests` class instead of appending into the XCTestCase that *is*
the test fixture of the type (`SiteObserverTests`). seat appends there.
`Type()` is only the fallback when no such class exists.

Default stdout is the existing test file with owed methods seated. `--check`
lists ranked worlds without writing. `--no-follow` is hatch. `--no-rank` is
till. `--no-construct` is seep. `--no-seat` is loam (sibling class).

`--report` is the sow listing. `--apply` writes into the existing file.
`--diff` is a unified diff against it. Machine visa is a skip *comment* only,
never the object.

Exit codes:
  0  ok (or --check with no due fixtures)
  1  --check found one or more due fixtures
  2  usage / tool error
"""
